        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 139 adds support for the <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#attr-button-command-request-close\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">request-close</code></a> value of the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> element's <code class=\"notranslate\">command</code> attribute. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5592399713402880\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5592399713402880</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">BCD also includes a data point for the same value on the <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLButtonElement.command</code> DOM property.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds this data to the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> element too, so it is available there.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
